<h2>Project Overview</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 30%;">Project Name</th>
    <td><strong>CampusTrace</strong> (College Lost &amp; Found Portal)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <th>Startup Inspiration</th>
    <td><strong>Boomerang</strong> (Y Combinator S22 / Product Hunt #1 Product of the Day)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <th>Tech Stack</th>
    <td>Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, Tailwind CSS, React Context API, Lucide Icons</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <th>Team Structure</th>
    <td>
      <strong>Student 1 (Architecture Lead):</strong> Next.js Setup, React Context Engine, Security Desk (/admin), Authentication<br>
      <strong>Student 2 (UI Lead):</strong> Design System, Landing Page, Reusable Component Library, Forms, Dummy Dataset
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>Key Deliverables Included in GitHub Repository</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>PRODUCT-ASSUMPTIONS.md:</strong> Complete 8-question product assumption and scope document.</li>
  <li><strong>DESIGN-SYSTEM.md:</strong> Color tokens (#2563EB), typography scale (Inter), and 12 reusable UI component tokens.</li>
  <li><strong>WIREFRAME.md:</strong> Complete page blueprints, information architecture, and user flows.</li>
  <li><strong>PROJECT-PLAN.md:</strong> 14 GitHub Issues breakdown with student assignments and git workflow.</li>
  <li><strong>Working Next.js Application:</strong> Fully functioning frontend with real-time directory search, campus filters, report forms, anti-fraud claim verification, and custody desk administration.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How to Run Locally from GitHub</h2>
<ol style="padding-left: 20pt; font-size: 10.5pt;">
  <li><code>git clone https://github.com/thanzeer-tech/lost-and-found.git</code></li>
  <li><code>cd lost-and-found</code></li>
  <li><code>npm install</code></li>
  <li><code>npm run dev</code></li>
  <li>Open <code>http://localhost:3000</code> in your browser.</li>
</ol>

</body>
